From 8f64602f77cb7dc306a259973a51a743e457e54f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hojin12312 <hojin12312@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:27:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] perf(qwen35): read Q8 scales and biases in the checkpoint
 layout for W8A8 prefill

The Q8 W8A8 prefill kernel needed the group scales and biases transposed to
[K/64, N], which kept a second copy of them for every Q8 projection (1.416 GiB
on Qwen3.8-27B). This adds a Q8 kernel that reads them as the checkpoint stores
them, [N, K/64], and routes every Q8 projection to it, so the copy is never
built.

The kernel swaps the tensor-op operands: weights are the left input and tokens
the right one. A lane then accumulates four weight rows, the rows whose codes
it already loads, so a group's scale and bias are scalar loads, and the
token-side values become four-wide loads. There is no threadgroup memory and no
barrier. The arithmetic per element is unchanged, so the output is bit-identical
to the group-major kernel, which stays in the tree as the reference the tests
compare against. Q4/Q5, decode and MTP paths are untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
